From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:03:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 328/342] usb: read a configuration again when its descriptors
 come back broken

On the test board an AB13X whose hub port was switched off and on during
playback answered with broken lengths among its configuration's
descriptors (255, 109, 101: "invalid descriptor length ... ignoring"):
the parse stopped there and its drivers got a configuration without the
interfaces and endpoints after it, which usb_audio's replug and new
device paths both tripped over (kernel page faults at 0x30 and 0x6).

After reading the full configuration, its descriptor chain is checked; if
a descriptor's length is broken, it is read again every 250 ms for up to
2 seconds, before parsing what there is as before. In 15 replugs during
playback, 9 of 10 broken reads were whole on the first read again, one
not after 300 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp        | 27 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
index 14c167fdb4..fb4f8270f2 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/usb/Device.cpp
@@ -127,8 +127,31 @@ Device::Device(Object* parent, int8 hubAddress, uint8 hubPort,
 			return;
 		}
 
-		status = GetDescriptor(USB_DESCRIPTOR_CONFIGURATION, i, 0,
-			(void*)configData, configDescriptor.total_length, &actualLength);
+		// A device just powered on (a replug, a port powered again) may still
+		// be settling and answer with a broken descriptor length among its
+		// descriptors (an AB13X gave 255, 109, 101): the parse below would
+		// stop there and hand its drivers a configuration without the
+		// interfaces after it. Read it again for up to 2 seconds first.
+		for (int32 attempt = 0; attempt < 8; attempt++) {
+			if (attempt > 0) {
+				TRACE_ERROR("configuration %" B_PRId32 " descriptors broken,"
+					" reading them again\n", i);
+				snooze(250000);
+			}
+			status = GetDescriptor(USB_DESCRIPTOR_CONFIGURATION, i, 0,
+				(void*)configData, configDescriptor.total_length,
+				&actualLength);
+			if (status < B_OK || actualLength != configDescriptor.total_length)
+				break;
+
+			uint32 offset = sizeof(usb_configuration_descriptor);
+			while (offset + 2 <= actualLength && configData[offset] >= 2
+				&& offset + configData[offset] <= actualLength) {
+				offset += configData[offset];
+			}
+			if (offset == actualLength)
+				break;
+		}
 
 		if (status < B_OK || actualLength != configDescriptor.total_length) {
 			TRACE_ERROR("error fetching full configuration"
